    "body": "I was trying to research how to get the class bound method instead of the function in a decorator and was looking at attrs if it figured it out, but apparently not\n```python\n>>> import attrs\n\n... @attrs.define\n... class A:\n...     foo: str = attrs.field()\n... \n...     @foo.default\n...     def _foo_default(self):\n...         return \"A\"\n... \n... @attrs.define\n... class B(A):\n...     def _foo_default(self):\n...         return \"B\"\n... print(A())\n... print(B())\nA(foo='A')\nB(foo='A')  # was expecting `foo='B'` here due to overriding\n```\n\nHave you guys researched this topic and is there any conclusions on this?",
